    "narrative": "Our premier plays today center on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.15) and **Gunnar Henderson** (65.73). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a solid matchup against a lefty in Shane McClanahan, where his power profile effectively mitigates the platoon disadvantage. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a high-output game batting second against Weathers; he remains our most reliable anchor. While **Coby Mayo** (61.43) is currently slated in the UTIL slot, he is performing as a top-tier asset today due to the same park-induced offensive boost as **Gunnar Henderson**, providing excellent value from the bottom third of the lineup. **Jackson Merrill** (59.11) also merits attention; despite the slight penalty for elite opposing hold skills, his projected stolen base volume makes him a high-floor start for our SB-starved roster.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Heliot Ramos** (45.34), who was edged out of the active lineup by the superior matchup context for **Wade Meckler** and **Liam Hicks**. While **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a slow opposing delivery that usually aids his steal efficiency, his overall efficiency score dipped behind the surging projections of our starting outfielders. We are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, specifically for **Liam Hicks**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Wade Meckler**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Coby Mayo**. Should these players shift into lower-leverage spots or hit the bench, we will be forced to reconsider our defensive integrity. Note that **Jordan Westburg** and **Jacob Wilson** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our middle infield depth limited as we push for 5x5 category gains.",
